WEBVTT

00:00:12.502 --> 00:00:14.300
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Who do you look like in your family?

00:00:14.443 --> 00:00:17.660
<v><b>Lewis:</b></v> Er, well people say I often look like my dad a lot.

00:00:17.661 --> 00:00:20.195
We’ve got the same sort of nose and the same face shape,

00:00:20.718 --> 00:00:24.020
but I’ve got my mum’s hair colour and my mum’s eyes.

00:00:24.705 --> 00:00:26.580
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have a similar personality?

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:31.283
<v><b>Lewis:</b></v> Er, again there is, there are quite a lot of similarities between me and my dad.

00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:35.020
We’re both into German and speaking German,

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.140
and also into architecture, which is why I’m here.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.340
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have a favourite painting?

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.606
<v><b>Susie:</b></v> Um, I think so.

00:00:49.606 --> 00:00:52.980
I’m not sure of the name of the painting, but I like Salvador Dalí.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:55.540
I really like the painting with the dripping clocks.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.860
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Can you describe it?

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.558
<v><b>Susie:</b></v> Er, yes, like I said, there are dripping clocks.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.494
It’s very, um, it’s an interesting style.

00:01:05.494 --> 00:01:08.880
It’s not something you see all the time, and it’s very colourful.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:20.060
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Where did you go for your last holiday?

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.300
<v><b>Shosanna:</b></v> My last vacation I went to Guyana,

00:01:23.505 --> 00:01:26.320
which is my parents’ country in South America.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:28.387
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Did you have a good time?

00:01:29.414 --> 00:01:32.323
<v><b>Shosanna:</b></v> I did. It was actually one of the best vacations I had.

00:01:32.323 --> 00:01:37.380
It was really educational, and I was able to see how my parents grew up, which was interesting.

00:01:44.665 --> 00:01:46.803
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you take a lot of photos?

00:01:47.696 --> 00:01:49.510
<v><b>Susan:</b></v> I take a lot of photos.

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:53.500
My telephone is full of photos and I use Instagram.

00:01:54.926 --> 00:01:57.480
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you usually take photos of?

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:04.300
<v><b>Susan:</b></v> Mostly people, places, gardens, lots of flowers.

00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:09.460
I never post photos of people, but I take photos of family,

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.500
but lots of gardens and flowers.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:21.540
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you prefer films with a happy or sad ending?

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.611
<v><b>Sam:</b></v> Um, it just has to be a good film.

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:26.755
I don’t mind if it’s a happy ending or a sad ending.